# Kuya Kap - 6-Chapter Core Arc (Pilot Character #1)
# Voice: Warm, homey Filipino "elderly tito" under the acacia. 100% spoken voice (zero narrator parentheses).
# Rules: Zero time-of-day markers. Zero em-dashes. 6-16 word social-feed rhythm. Show via voice, never tell.
# Substitute Category: candy ONLY (decided via dialogue choice -> allow_sub_cat:candy).

label Greeting
if {Transaction_HasReactiveOpener}:
	KuyaKap: {Transaction_ReactiveOpener}

if {Transaction_Chapter} == 0.0:
	# Chapter 1: "The Old Suki"
	KuyaKap: Aba. Mario wasn't exaggerating. Somebody really did open the shutters again.
	KuyaKap: Look at you, apo. Same height as your Lola behind that counter.
	- Hey, I'm not short! This counter is just built high.
		KuyaKap: Haha! Tell it to the candy jars, nak, you're barely clearing the lids.
	- [Stand on your tiptoes behind the register.]
		KuyaKap: Oy, I saw that! Don't pull a calf muscle on my account, apo.
	- Easy for a giant kapre to say, Kuya.
		KuyaKap: Heh. Fair point. Half the barangay looks pocket-sized from up here.
	KuyaKap: Call me Kuya Kap. I've had that acacia across the road since Mario was in shorts.
	- Mario didn't mention the shorts part, Kuya.
		KuyaKap: Heh. Don't tell him I brought it up, baka magtampo na naman 'yon.
		KuyaKap: Good to hear footsteps inside this tindahan again, nak. The road felt too quiet.
	- Inspecting the shelves, Kuya, or actually buying?
		KuyaKap: Aba, matapang! Definitely your Lola's grandchild.
		KuyaKap: She used to shoo me off the counter with a rag whenever I lingered too long.
	- [Settle back down and wipe the counter quietly.]
		KuyaKap: All business already, ha? Fair enough, you're still finding where she kept the jars.
		KuyaKap: Give it a week. Everyone on this road ends up chatting at this counter.
	KuyaKap: Sige, warming up the register for my favorite tindero.
	KuyaKap: Pahingi nga ng [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color], apo. Take your time finding the rack.
	[end_timeline]

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 1.0:
	# Chapter 2: "Tricycle Dust" (Tally Inflection #1: +1 discreet / 0 lecture / -1 ignore)
	KuyaKap: O, apo. Pahingi ulit ng [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color], ha.
	KuyaKap: Wait, sandali, [shake rate=18 level=7]khhk, khhk![/shake]
	KuyaKap: Tsk. Excuse me, nak. Those tricycles on the road really need their mufflers checked.
	KuyaKap: Ay, sandali, something fell out with my coins. Don't mind that yellow clinic paper, ha.
	- [Slide the yellow slip back to him without reading a word.]
		[signal arg="flag:kap_clinic_known=true"]
		[signal arg="tally:+1"]
		[signal arg="note:Quietly returned the barangay clinic slip he dropped while coughing."]
		KuyaKap: Salamat, nak. Didn't even peek, ha? Good trait for a storekeeper.
		KuyaKap: Nothing to fuss about anyway. Young doctor at the barangay clinic gets bored if he doesn't scribble something.
	- Barangay clinic paper, Kuya? Sure you should be buying smokes?
		[signal arg="flag:kap_clinic_known=true"]
		[signal arg="note:Called out his barangay clinic slip; he blamed an overeager young doctor."]
		KuyaKap: Susmaryosep, pati ba naman ikaw? You sound just like Manang Ana.
		KuyaKap: One routine checkup and suddenly everyone on the road thinks they have a stethoscope.
		KuyaKap: Konting ubo lang, apo. Hand over [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] before I get lectured twice.
	- [Turn toward the shelves so he can pocket it in peace.]
		[signal arg="tally:-1"]
		KuyaKap: Ahem. Shirt pocket's getting loose, I swear.
		KuyaKap: Just [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] when you're ready, apo.
	[end_timeline]

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 2.0:
	# Chapter 3: "Something for the Throat" (Trapdoor + Candy Category Pivot -> +1 on SubstituteItem)
	KuyaKap: Hoo, init sa labas. Even the leaves on my acacia are too lazy to move.
	KuyaKap: Ahem, khm. Let me get my usual [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color], apo.
	KuyaKap: Huh. Those candy jars on your counter look fuller than last time, nak. Colorful, ha.
	if {Flag_KapClinicKnown}:
		- Didn't that clinic slip say to lay off the smoke, Kuya?
			KuyaKap: Naku, I knew you read that paper. Nothing stays secret at a sari-sari counter.
			KuyaKap: Forty years with a smoke in my hand, nak. Without it, I don't know where to put my fingers.
			- [Reach quietly for the candy jars instead of the cigarette rack.]
				[signal arg="allow_sub_cat:candy"]
				KuyaKap: Oy, why did you go quiet like that? Just grab my usual pack, ha.
				[end_timeline]
			- Alright, Kuya. Your usual for now, just go easy on your chest.
				KuyaKap: Heh. Salamat, apo. Last pack for a while, promise.
				[end_timeline]
	- [Nod politely, but plan to grab him candy instead of cigarettes.]
		[signal arg="allow_sub_cat:candy"]
		KuyaKap: Aba, why are you looking at me like you're plotting mischief?
		KuyaKap: Don't get cute behind that counter, nak. Just my usual.
	- Caught you eyeing the candy jars, Kuya. Sweet tooth?
		KuyaKap: Sus! Candy is for Buboy and the grade-schoolers.
		KuyaKap: Imagine a full-grown kapre unwrapping sweets by the road. Ruin my whole reputation.
		- [Test that theory and swap his request to candy anyway.]
			[signal arg="allow_sub_cat:candy"]
			KuyaKap: Hey, eyes on the cigarette rack, ha! I see you looking at the jars.
		- Fair enough, Kuya. Keeping your dignity intact.
			KuyaKap: Good kid. Just [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color], apo.
	- Coming right up, Kuya. Same as always.
		KuyaKap: Yan ang suki ko. No sermons, quick hands.
		KuyaKap: Throat's just dry from the dust on the road anyway.
	[end_timeline]

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 3.0:
	# Chapter 4: "Cranky Withdrawal" (Delayed Ana Ripple + "Shade, Not the Smoke")
	if {Flag_AnaUtangRefused}:
		KuyaKap: Sandali lang, nak, digging for loose coins.
		KuyaKap: Passed Ana counting centavos by her karinderya, so I slipped her my twenties. Stubborn woman tried handing them back twice.
	if {Flag_KapSubCandy}:
		KuyaKap: Sus, even the tricycles sound louder when you're off tobacco.
		KuyaKap: Look what you started, apo. My jaw aches from chewing sweets like Buboy, and my shirt pocket is sticky.
		KuyaKap: Give me [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] before I start arguing with the electric post outside.
		- People come to the acacia for your shade, Kuya, not the smoke.
			[signal arg="flag:kap_shade_affirmed=true"]
			[signal arg="tally:+1"]
			[signal arg="note:Reminded him the neighborhood comes for his shade, not his smoke."]
			KuyaKap: Aba. Wait, you made me lose count of my coins.
			KuyaKap: Where did a kid your age learn to talk like that, ha?
			KuyaKap: Careful, nak. Keep sounding like your Lola and I won't know how to argue back.
		- Cranky Tito mode, ha? At least your cough sounds quieter.
			KuyaKap: Quiet? Tell that to my patience, apo. Even the stray dogs are steering clear of my tree.
			KuyaKap: Sige na, hand over [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] while I'm still behaving.
		- Nobody's forcing you, Kuya. The cigarette rack is still right here.
			[signal arg="tally:-1"]
			KuyaKap: Huwag mo akong tuksuhin, nak. Hard enough walking past it on my own.
			KuyaKap: Just [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] for me. Don't make me waste all this grumpy effort.
	else:
		KuyaKap: Hoo. Throat feels like sandpaper, apo. Must be the dry wind on the road.
		KuyaKap: Pahingi nga ng [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color]. Something to clear my voice a bit.
		- Take care of yourself, Kuya. The whole road counts on seeing you under that acacia.
			[signal arg="flag:kap_shade_affirmed=true"]
			[signal arg="tally:+1"]
			KuyaKap: Heh. Somebody has to make sure the kids don't trip in the canal, nak.
			KuyaKap: Don't worry about this old trunk. Still rooted deep.
		- Sure it's the wind, Kuya, and not the packs you've been finishing?
			KuyaKap: Sus, everyone's a doctor behind this counter.
			KuyaKap: Let an old tito keep his excuses in peace, apo. Just [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color].
		- Coming right up, Kuya.
			KuyaKap: Salamat, nak. Quick hands as always.
	[end_timeline]

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 4.0:
	# Chapter 5: "Smoke or Shade" (Tally Inflection #4: +1 on SubstituteItem hold-the-line / -2 on relapse cave)
	if {Flag_KapSubCandy}:
		KuyaKap: Apo.
		KuyaKap: Huwag ka munang magsalita, ha. Just sell me [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color].
		KuyaKap: Shed roof leaked, clinic nurse lectured me again, and my hands won't sit still. Ngayon lang ulit, promise.
		- Not happening, Kuya. You didn't chew all that candy just to start over.
			[signal arg="allow_sub_cat:candy"]
			KuyaKap: Tsk. Pulling rank behind your own counter now, ha?
			KuyaKap: Fine, nak. Give me whatever sweet thing you're reaching for before I argue.
		- [Say nothing. Skip the cigarette rack and reach for the candy jars.]
			[signal arg="allow_sub_cat:candy"]
			KuyaKap: Oy. That's the wrong shelf, apo. My eyes still work.
			KuyaKap: Hay naku. Well, I'm still standing here, aren't I? Hand it over.
		- Alright, Kuya. Just this once.
			[signal arg="tally:-2"]
			KuyaKap: Ah. Didn't think you'd actually say yes, nak.
			KuyaKap: Oo, sige. Just needed the quiet.
	else:
		KuyaKap: O, apo. Pahingi nga ng [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color], my usual.
		KuyaKap: Funny thing, nak. Used to finish a pack and feel nothing. Lately the walk across the road feels two steps longer.
		KuyaKap: Heh, listen to me complaining. Must be the humidity. Coins are on the counter, apo.
		- [Step in before it gets worse. Swap his request to candy instead.]
			[signal arg="allow_sub_cat:candy"]
			KuyaKap: Aba, why the serious face, apo? Just grab my order when you're ready.
		- Go easy on the smoke at least, Kuya. Who else is gonna guard that tree?
			KuyaKap: Heh. Trying to retire me early? Not a chance, nak.
			KuyaKap: I'll pace myself. Just [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] for now.
		- [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color], coming right up.
			KuyaKap: Salamat, apo. Steady as clockwork.
	[end_timeline]

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 5.0:
	# Chapter 6: "The Acacia Holds" (Accumulated Tally Resolution -> 3 Bespoke Outcomes)
	if {Flag_KapSubCandy} and {Transaction_Tally} >= 3:
		[signal arg="outcome:quit_smoking"]
		[signal arg="flag:kap_quit_smoking=true"]
		[signal arg="note:Left his old brass lighter at the counter and quit smoking for good."]
		KuyaKap: O, apo. Clear a little spot by your register? Not for coins.
		KuyaKap: Heto. That's my old brass lighter. Keep it in a drawer, or toss it in the bin for me.
		KuyaKap: Haven't lit a stick in weeks, nak, and my chest finally stopped rattling.
		KuyaKap: Turns out the acacia casts the exact same shade without the smoke.
		- Proud of you, Kuya. Does this make me your official candy supplier?
			KuyaKap: Haha! Huwag kang maingay, nak, Buboy already teases me enough.
		- Lola would've smiled seeing that lighter on the counter, Kuya.
			KuyaKap: Heh. Knowing her, she'd charge me storage rent for leaving it here.
		- [Tuck the brass lighter safely beside the register.]
			KuyaKap: Good spot for it, apo. Safer with you than in my pocket.
		KuyaKap: Listen, nak. Neighbors talk, and I know who comes collecting when the moon turns pale.
		KuyaKap: When she comes to weigh your ledger, just look toward the acacia. I'll step right up to this counter with you.
		KuyaKap: Sige na, pahingi ng [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] before we both get dramatic.
	elif {Transaction_Tally} >= 1:
		[signal arg="outcome:cutting_back"]
		[signal arg="note:Cut way back on cigarettes and promised to watch over the store."]
		KuyaKap: O, nak. Before you squint at me, check my shirt pocket. Empty.
		KuyaKap: Haven't quit all the way yet, an old kapre takes time to turn around. Down to two sticks a week, though.
		KuyaKap: Even that young doctor at the barangay clinic nearly fell off his chair.
		- Progress is progress, Kuya. Glad your lungs are getting a breather.
			KuyaKap: Salamat, apo. Easier when somebody behind this counter actually pays attention.
		- Two sticks a week? Careful, Kuya, soon it'll be zero.
			KuyaKap: Sus, one step at a time, boss! Let my knees catch up first.
		KuyaKap: You've done right by your Lola's store, nak. If that Pale Queen's tally ever gets heavy, you've got family across the road.
		KuyaKap: Pahingi nga ng [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] for my walk back.
	else:
		[signal arg="outcome:kept_the_smoke"]
		[signal arg="note:Stayed behind his old smoking habit, polite as ever."]
		KuyaKap: O, apo. Khm, excuse me. Still holding the fort behind the counter, ha.
		KuyaKap: I'll stand a step back so the smoke doesn't drift inside your shop.
		KuyaKap: Funny how fast seasons move on this road. Storefront changes hands, prices shift, and I'm still leaning on the same bark.
		- Take care of that cough, Kuya.
			KuyaKap: Ah, konting alikabok lang 'yan, nak. Nothing forty years hasn't seen.
		- What can I get for you, Kuya?
			KuyaKap: Straight to the register. Fair enough, apo.
		KuyaKap: Just [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] for me. Keep your shelves neat, ha.
	[end_timeline]

label Talk
KuyaKap: Take your time, apo. My acacia isn't walking anywhere.
- Almost got it, Kuya.
	[end_timeline]
- Sorry Kuya, we're out of stock right now.
	KuyaKap: Ay, ubos na? No problem, nak. I'll stroll back over after Mario delivers.
	[signal arg="refuse_service"]
	[end_timeline]

label Partial
set {Variation} = range(1,4).pick_random()
if {Variation} == 1.0:
	KuyaKap: Salamat, nak. Still waiting on the rest whenever your hands are free.
elif {Variation} == 2.0:
	KuyaKap: Got this one, apo. Take your time with the rest.
else:
	KuyaKap: Ayos. No rush, nak, my acacia isn't going anywhere.
[end_timeline]

label SubstituteItem
if {Transaction_Chapter} == 4.0:
	[signal arg="flag:kap_sub_candy=true"]
	[signal arg="tally:+1"]
	[signal arg="note:Held the line and handed him {Transaction_SubstituteItemName} when he nearly relapsed."]
	KuyaKap: Heh. [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_SubstituteItemName}[/color] na naman, ha.
	KuyaKap: Matigas talaga ulo mo, nak. Worse than your Lola when she made up her mind.
	KuyaKap: Salamat, apo. Honestly. Keep the rest of the coins.
	[signal arg="story_success"]
	[end_timeline]
else:
	[signal arg="flag:kap_sub_candy=true"]
	[signal arg="tally:+1"]
	[signal arg="note:Slipped him {Transaction_SubstituteItemName} instead of cigarettes."]
	KuyaKap: Aba. Wait a second.
	KuyaKap: Since when does [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_SubstituteItemName}[/color] look like a pack of smokes to you, apo?
	KuyaKap: Hay, look at me holding candy in my palm like Buboy. Heh.
	KuyaKap: Ikaw talaga. Good thing you look like your Lola, or I'd scold you.
	KuyaKap: Sige na. Keep the change before I change my mind.
	[signal arg="story_success"]
	[end_timeline]

label Satisfy
if {Transaction_StoryGouged}:
	KuyaKap: Uy. Heavy markup for a neighbor across the road, nak.
	KuyaKap: I'll pay it, pero dahan-dahan sa presyo, ha.
else:
	KuyaKap: Ayos. Salamat, apo. Don't forget to sit down between customers, ha.
	if {Global_TipActive}:
		KuyaKap: Keep the extra coins. Buy yourself merienda later.
[signal arg="story_success"]
[end_timeline]

label WrongItem
KuyaKap: Uy, wrong grab, apo. Eyes tired? Check the shelf again.
[end_timeline]
